responded by scaling data and models rather than fixing the

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:27.774
The paper's move is to ask the question nobody had answered.

00:02:28.224 --> 00:02:36.312
Not how to avoid collapse, but what distribution the
embeddings should follow — and then derive the mechanism from

00:02:37.662 --> 00:02:40.830
Here is how they make that question answerable.

